	"description": [
		"In this course, students study the evolving relationship between Eastern Orthodox cultures and the political authorities with which they interact. They explore how changing imperial structures, primarily in the regions of the Middle East, Southeastern Europe, and Russia, have forced an ongoing reconsideration of how religion and state power relate to each other. Offered periodically during spring semester."
